    "result_text": "Only one test class exists, and it passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a read-time derived field on the owner response \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the decimal digits of `customerCode`, matching the existing pattern for computed fields like `locality`, `identityKey`, and `contactPreference`.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`CustomerCodeCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 helper computing the Luhn check digit over the digits in an owner's `customerCode` (non-digit characters like `LON-SMI-` are skipped, so it's derived from the numeric portion). Returns `null` when no customer code is set.\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(CustomerCodeCheckDigit.of(owner))\")` plus the import.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 it passes, as does the full suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
